   "subject": "Hierarchical regression with a within-subjects factor",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I recently asked this question on <a href=\"http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/92064/within-subjects-model-in-jags-stan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/92064/within-subjects-model-in-jags-stan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466743297000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hOGyFMHAYAiuLM50WGNgC\">Cross-validated</a>, but I think I&#39;ll have more luck here, as it&#39;s probably too software-related:<div><br></div><div>I have data from a psychophysical experiment, in which I tested S subjects in J=2 conditions (within-subjects design). I am trying to model each subject&#39;s probability of giving a (binary) response y as a function of a stimulus parameter x; a standard approach is to use the cumulative normal density function as a psychometric function, which means that I&#39;m using a probit regression model.</div><div><br></div><div>Each observation is modelled as a mixture of Bernoulli distributions: either the subject does as he/she is supposed to or has an attentional lapse with a certain probability and then has to guess:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bernoulli</span><span style=\"color:#660\">((</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> guess</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div>Intercepts and slopes are allowed to vary by condition nested within subject. My aim is to estimate group-level intercept and slope parameters for each condition. <div><br></div><div>The problem I&#39;m having is how to allow for the fact that alpha and beta are correlated, and, additionally, the parameters for each condition are correlated for each subject, i.e. if subject A has a high alpha in condition 1, then also in condition 2.</div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone have any recommendations on the best way to go about this? It&#39;s probably quite a simple problem, but it&#39;s got me stumped for the moment. </div><div><br></div><div>I have included a minimal working model, plus dataset (for 6 subjects) and R code. I deliberately omitted all correlations between parameters, and the model is pretty much a translation from JAGS code, so all the loops are still in there.<br><div><br></div><div>Full stan model:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of observations</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of conditions</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of subjects</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// response</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// condition index variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// subject index variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// test orientation (covariate)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//varying intercept</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//varying slope</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//subject-specific lapse rate</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> guess</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//subject-specific guessing parameter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// group-level intercept</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_alpha_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// group-level slope</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_beta_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// subject-specific lapse and guessing parameters</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        guess</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// loop over conditions</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// loop over </span><span style=\"color:#800\">subjects</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_alpha_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_beta_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        alpha_g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e02</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// non-informative prior on group-level intercept</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        beta_g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e02</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// non-informative prior on group-level slope</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bernoulli</span><span style=\"color:#660\">((</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]])*</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                     lapse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">guess</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
